mode: "100644"
text: "Software Engineer III, Infrastructure, Google Cloud\nGoogle · Mountain View, CA, USA · Hybrid\n\n<!-- Example job description for hunter-skill. Written for this pack in the format of Google's public job postings (Minimum qualifications, Preferred qualifications, About the job, Responsibilities). The format was checked on 2026-10-15 against a live Google Cloud infrastructure posting: https://www.google.com/about/careers/applications/jobs/results/79605303951139526-software-engineer-iii-infrastructure-google-cloud-platforms . This text is NOT a real Google posting, and it states no pay range. -->\n\nMinimum qualifications:\n- Bachelor's degree or equivalent practical experience.\n- 2 years of experience with software development in Go, C++ or Java.\n- 2 years of experience building distributed systems.\n- 2 years of experience with data structures or algorithms.\n\nPreferred qualifications:\n- Master's degree or PhD in Computer Science or a related technical field.\n- Experience with Kubernetes, containers and Google Cloud Platform.\n- Experience with machine learning systems, ranking or recommendations.\n- Experience improving the latency, performance and reliability of production services.\n- Experience with on-call, incident response and runbooks.\n\nAbout the job\nGoogle Cloud's infrastructure teams build the compute, storage and networking that customers run their businesses on. In this role you will work on a service at the core of Google Cloud, with the chance to switch teams and projects as you and the business grow.\n\nResponsibilities\n- Write and test product or system development code in Go.\n- Participate in, or lead, design reviews with peers and stakeholders.\n- Do code reviews for other engineers and give feedback on testing and style.\n- Triage production issues and debug them, then improve monitoring so they do not recur.\n- Mentor newer engineers and contribute to documentation.\n"
